SolarWinds provides multiple types of agent installations for monitoring devices, depending on the environment and use case. Here’s a breakdown of the agent types and the ports they use for communication:

1. Agent-Based Monitoring
SolarWinds uses Orion Agents to collect data from remote devices when SNMP or WMI is not ideal. Agents are installed on the target machine and send data to the SolarWinds server.
Agent Installation Types:
	1. Agent-Initiated Mode (Pull Mode)
		○ The agent on the monitored device initiates communication with the SolarWinds server.
		○ Best for remote systems or devices behind firewalls.
