Orion Agent - Agent-Initiated Mode in SolarWinds
The Agent-Initiated Mode is one of the deployment options for Orion Agents in SolarWinds. In this mode, the agent installed on the monitored device establishes and maintains communication with the SolarWinds Orion Server, rather than the server reaching out to the agent. This is useful for remote devices, firewalled environments, or cloud-based systems where inbound connections to the device are restricted.

How Agent-Initiated Mode Works
	• The agent establishes an outbound connection to the SolarWinds Orion server.
	• It sends status updates and data at regular intervals.
	• The server does not need direct access to the agent, making it firewall-friendly.

Ports Used in Agent-Initiated Mode
Port	Protocol	Description
TCP 17778	HTTPS	Primary communication between the agent and Orion server (encrypted).
TCP 17790	Optional	Used for real-time commands and interactive agent communication.
Since the agent initiates the connection, only outbound traffic from the monitored device to the SolarWinds server needs to be allowed.

How to Install and Configure Orion Agent (Agent-Initiated Mode)
Step 1: Open Agent Management in SolarWinds Orion
	1. Log in to your SolarWinds Orion Web Console.
	2. Go to Settings → All Settings → Manage Agents.
	3. Click Add Agent.
Step 2: Choose Deployment Method
	1. Select Deploy Agent on a Node.
	2. Choose Agent-Initiated Mode.
	3. Enter the Orion Server’s IP Address or Hostname.
	4. Click Next.
Step 3: Install the Agent on the Target Device
	• You can install the agent in multiple ways:
		1. Push Install – If the device is on the network and accessible.
		2. Manual Install – Download the agent installer from Orion and run it on the device.
